name: the machine
boss: Spectrum
flavor: It is all in the air, and someone is always listening.
brief: Every machine will tell you what it is, if you ask. `uname` names the
brief: kernel, `dmesg` carries what the kernel said while booting, and `/proc` and
brief: `/sys` are the kernel's own filesystem -- files that are not on any disk.
brief:
brief: `/proc` is the habit worth forming. Nearly everything a monitoring tool
brief: reports, it read out of a file in there, and so can you.
brief:
brief: The rest of the asking: `hostname` is its name, `date` the software clock
brief: and `hwclock` the battery-backed one under it, `lspci` `lsusb` and `lsscsi`
brief: list what is plugged into which bus, `devmem` reads physical memory by
brief: address, `logger` writes your own line into the log `dmesg` reads, `watch`
brief: reruns a command so you can see a number move.
brief:
brief: The terminal is a device too: `tty` names yours, `stty` sets how it behaves,
brief: `clear` tidies it and `reset` rescues it after a binary has left it speaking
brief: garbage, `loadkmap` and `dumpkmap` load and save the keyboard map, `script`
brief: and `scriptreplay` record a session and play it back. `microcom` talks to a
brief: serial port -- the way in when the network is gone.
---
